{"type":"text","timestamp":1794372932476,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8f6134d001lRUYIv1rHc9lR0","messageID":"msg_1c8f5f707001Y64Ss6Z6PxQq9v","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"text","text":"<think>Wait — there's an issue with the catch-all route `/<path:path>` and the `/api/...` routes: the `/api/health` static rule vs. catch-all. Werkzeug should match the static rule first. But `/api/unknown` would match the catch-all → handled by my `path.startswith(\"api/\")` check → 404 JSON. Good.\n\nBut wait: `@app.get(\"/\")` and `@app.get(\"/<path:path>\")` — the \"/\" rule with default arg path=\"index.html\". OK.\n\nAnother issue: `payload()` uses request.form.to_dict() → returns ImmutableMultiDict values as strings. Fine.\n\nIssue: `as_number` for bool returns None → \"value must be a number\". Good.\n\nIssue: In `logout`, `header.split(None, 1)[1].strip() if \" \" in header else \"\"` — if header is \"Bearer abc\", split(None,1) → [\"Bearer\", \"abc\"] → [1]=\"abc\". Good. If header is \"abc\" (no space) → \"\". Fine.\n\nNow, `init_db()` is called at import time — good for gunicorn.\n\nOne concern: `g.user` set in require_user — `g` is flask.g. Fine.\n\nAnother: In `require_user`, I call `current_user()` which uses request headers.\n\nPotential issue: Flask's `jsonify` of tuple return `(jsonify(...), status)` works.\n\nNow `serialize_sensor(row)` when row is None (create_sensor fetch) — row should exist. Fine.\n\nType annotation `Callable[..., Any]` import from typing — fine.\n\nLet me now test the backend quickly.\n\nAlso: `from __future__ import annotations` with `float | None` annotations on 3.13 — fine.\n\nLet's writea quick test script.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794372932429,"end":1794372932447}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794372932476,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c8f6044972e58c04ba6a","state":{"status":"error","input":{"command":"cd /workspace && rm -rf /tmp/opencode/testdata && DATA_DIR=/tmp/opencode/testdata python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json, os\nos.environ.setdefault(\"DATA_DIR\", \"/tmp/opencode/testdata\")\nfrom backend.app import app\nc = app.test_client()\n\ndef show(label, r):\n    print(label, r.status_code, r.get_json())\n    return r\n\nshow(\"health\", c.get(\"/api/health\"))\nr = show(\"register\", c.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\":\"alice\",\"password\":\"pw\"}))\ntok = r.get_json()[\"token\"]\nH = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {tok}\"}\nshow(\"login\", c.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\":\"alice\",\"password\":\"pw\"}))\nshow(\"login-bad\", c.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\":\"alice\",\"password\":\"nope\"}))\nshow(\"reg-dup\", c.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\":\"alice\",\"password\":\"pw\"}))\nshow(\"noauth-post-sensor\", c.post(\"/api/sensors\", json={\"name\":\"x\"}))\nr = show(\"create sensor\", c.post(\"/api/sensors\", json={\"name\":\"Temp A\",\"unit\":\"C\",\"location\":\"Kitchen\"}, headers=H))\nsid = r.get_json()[\"id\"]\nshow(\"list sensors\", c.get(\"/api/sensors\"))\nshow(\"get sensor\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}\"))\nshow(\"post reading\", c.post(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings\", json={\"value\": 21.5}, headers=H))\nshow(\"post reading2\", c.post(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings\", json={\"value\": 23}, headers=H))\nshow(\"get sensor after\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}\"))\nshow(\"readings\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings\"))\nshow(\"readings limit\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings?limit=1\"))\nshow(\"readings bad limit\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings?limit=abc\"))\n# other user\nr2 = show(\"register bob\", c.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\":\"bob\",\"password\":\"pw\"}))\nH2 = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + r2.get_json()[\"token\"]}\nshow(\"bob post reading\", c.post(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings\", json={\"value\": 1}, headers=H2))\nshow(\"bob delete\", c.delete(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}\", headers=H2))\nshow(\"alice delete\", c.delete(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}\", headers=H))\nshow(\"readings after delete\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings\"))\nshow(\"404 sensor\", c.get(\"/api/sensors/999\"))\nPY"},"error":"The user has specified a rule which prevents you from using this specific tool call. Here are some of the relevant rules [{\"permission\":\"*\",\"action\":\"allow\",\"pattern\":\"*\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"*\",\"action\":\"ask\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"/run/home/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/*\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"/tmp/opencode/*\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"action\":\"deny\",\"pattern\":\"*\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"/run/home/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/*\",\"action\":\"allow\"}]","time":{"start":1794372932443,"end":1794372932456}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8f613510016PKheAkvQkZMVZ","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","messageID":"msg_1c8f5f707001Y64Ss6Z6PxQq9v"}}
