{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794372937392,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c8f61bfe732db9c99b38","state":{"status":"error","input":{"content":"import os\n\nos.environ.setdefault(\"DATA_DIR\", \"/tmp/opencode/testdata\")\n\nfrom backend.app import app  # noqa: E402\n\nc = app.test_client()\n\n\ndef show(label, r):\n    print(label, r.status_code, r.get_json())\n    return r\n\n\nshow(\"health\", c.get(\"/api/health\"))\nr = show(\"register\", c.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": \"alice\", \"password\": \"pw\"}))\ntok = r.get_json()[\"token\"]\nH = {\"Authorization\": f\"Bearer {tok}\"}\nshow(\"login\", c.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"alice\", \"password\": \"pw\"}))\nshow(\"login-bad\", c.post(\"/api/auth/login\", json={\"username\": \"alice\", \"password\": \"nope\"}))\nshow(\"reg-dup\", c.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": \"alice\", \"password\": \"pw\"}))\nshow(\"noauth-post-sensor\", c.post(\"/api/sensors\", json={\"name\": \"x\"}))\nr = show(\"create sensor\", c.post(\"/api/sensors\", json={\"name\": \"Temp A\", \"unit\": \"C\", \"location\": \"Kitchen\"}, headers=H))\nsid = r.get_json()[\"id\"]\nshow(\"list sensors\", c.get(\"/api/sensors\"))\nshow(\"get sensor\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}\"))\nshow(\"post reading\", c.post(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings\", json={\"value\": 21.5}, headers=H))\nshow(\"post reading2\", c.post(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings\", json={\"value\": 23}, headers=H))\nshow(\"get sensor after\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}\"))\nshow(\"readings\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings\"))\nshow(\"readings limit\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings?limit=1\"))\nshow(\"readings bad limit\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings?limit=abc\"))\nr2 = show(\"register bob\", c.post(\"/api/auth/register\", json={\"username\": \"bob\", \"password\": \"pw\"}))\nH2 = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + r2.get_json()[\"token\"]}\nshow(\"bob post reading\", c.post(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings\", json={\"value\": 1}, headers=H2))\nshow(\"bob delete\", c.delete(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}\", headers=H2))\nshow(\"alice delete\", c.delete(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}\", headers=H))\nshow(\"readings after delete\", c.get(f\"/api/sensors/{sid}/readings\"))\nshow(\"404 sensor\", c.get(\"/api/sensors/999\"))\nshow(\"api unknown\", c.get(\"/api/nope\"))\n","filePath":"/tmp/opencode/test_api.py"},"error":"The user has specified a rule which prevents you from using this specific tool call. Here are some of the relevant rules [{\"permission\":\"*\",\"action\":\"allow\",\"pattern\":\"*\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"*\",\"action\":\"ask\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"/run/home/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/*\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"/tmp/opencode/*\",\"action\":\"allow\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"action\":\"deny\",\"pattern\":\"*\"},{\"permission\":\"external_directory\",\"pattern\":\"/run/home/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/*\",\"action\":\"allow\"}]","time":{"start":1794372937355,"end":1794372937361}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8f626810016j4xR9rLl3cL5n","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","messageID":"msg_1c8f61376001EDYR6MO7KJ3ltK"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794372937392,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8f6267d001BK5Z8aT5KorMAF","messageID":"msg_1c8f61376001EDYR6MO7KJ3ltK","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"text","text":"<think>The heredoc with `cd /workspace` maybe triggered something? The rule denies external_directory except /tmp/opencode. Hmm, the command writes to /tmp/opencode/testdata which is allowed. Maybe the issue is that the command's cwd is /workspace... Actually the denial is likely because the python code writes files? Or maybe the `rm -rf /tmp/opencode/testdata` is fine.\n\nLet me instead write the test script to a file with the Write tool inside /workspace (e.g., /workspace/backend/test_api.py — but I'd rather not leave test files in the repo; I can delete afterwards or put in /tmp/opencode).\n\nLet me write the test file to /tmp/opencode/test_api.py and run it with workdir /workspace.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794372937341,"end":1794372937366}}}
