{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794373065404,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8f81aa6001eHN0Bn8MaEgsfm","messageID":"msg_1c8f7de92001SgSJnqk0aqPJLf","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794373065405,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8f81aa8001aCaIsxNVlubF5h","messageID":"msg_1c8f7de92001SgSJnqk0aqPJLf","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"text","text":"<think>Now the LineChart component.\n\nProps: readings: Reading[] (any order), unit: string, height.\n\nImplementation:\n- Points: readings.map(r => ({ t: new Date(r.recorded_at).getTime(), v: r.value })) filtered for valid times, sorted ascending by t.\n- If no points → empty state.\n- If all values equal → expand range by max(1, |v|*0.05).\n- X domain: min t to max t; if equal, use ± 1 minute.\n- Compute coordinates in viewBox space W=800, H=280 with padding {top:20,right:20,bottom:34,left:56}.\n- Y ticks: 5 lines with labels formatted.\n- X labels: earliest and latest time (formatClock) at the bottom.\n- Polyline + area fill (gradient) + dots.\n- Use `preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"` and `vectorEffect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"`.\n\nCareful: with preserveAspectRatio=\"none\", text would be stretched horizontally. That's ugly. Alternative: keep default preserveAspectRatio (meet) and let the SVG scale uniformly — the chart scales with the container width and keeps aspect ratio; height then varies. That's fine and simpler: `className=\"w-full h-auto\"` with viewBox → the SVG scales uniformly. Text remains readable.\n\nI'll use default preserveAspectRatio (xMidYMid meet) with `class=\"w-full\"` and viewBox aspect ratio 800x280 → rendered height = width * 0.35, capped by max-height. Hmm, on wide screens, the chart would be very tall (e.g., 1200px wide → 420px tall). That's acceptable but let me use `max-h-80`? With uniform scaling, `h-auto` plus max-h would distort? No: max-height with `w-full h-auto` on an SVG with viewBox → the SVG box is set by max-height and the content scales uniformly (meet), leaving horizontal empty space. Acceptable.\n\nSimpler approach: fixed CSS height (e.g., h-64) and preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" for the plot area only (the polyline/paths), while drawing axis labels as HTML outside the SVG. That's cleaner: the chart plot area is an SVG with preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" (fills the box, no distortion of the plot), and labels rendered as absolutely positioned HTML elements over the SVG.\n\nThat's more work but produces a nicer result. Let me do a hybrid:\n\n- Container: `relative w-full h-64`.\n- SVG absolute inset-0 with viewBox \"0 0 100 100\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" → x coordinates 0..100 map to width, y 0..100 map to height. Plot lines: y in 0..100 (top=0).\n- Axis labels: HTML absolutely positioned (left labels at left-0 translate -y, bottom labels at bottom).\n- Stroke width: use vectorEffect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" to avoid distortion.\n\nWith preserveAspectRatio=\"none\", a circle would become an ellipse. Use small rects? Instead of circles, use absolutely positioned HTML dots? Hmm. Alternative: draw dots as HTML divs positioned with left/top percentages — easy and crisp.\n\nPlan:\n- Plot area div: relative, h-64, w-full, with padding via CSS (left padding for y labels, bottom for x labels). Inside, an SVG (absolute inset-0) with viewBox 0 0 100 100 preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" drawing grid lines and the path, plus HTML dots positioned by percentage.\n- Y labels: absolutely positioned at left-0 (outside the plot div, so the plot div has margin-left ~ 48px).\n- X labels: below the plot.\n\nLet me structure:\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"w-full\">\n  <div className=\"relative h-64 pl-14\">\n    {/* y grid + labels */}\n    {ticks.map(t => (\n      <div key={t} className=\"absolute left-0 w-full -translate-y-1/2 ...\">  // label at left\n    ))}\n    ...\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\nSimpler approach with explicit layout:\n\n```tsx\nconst PLOT = { left: 56, top: 12, right: 12, bottom: 28 };  // px within a 100x100 viewBox? no\n```\n\nLet me use pixel viewBox: W=800, H=260, and use preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" only for the SVG, with the SVG container having a fixed aspect? Ugh.\n\nOK let me just use the percentage-based approach with an SVG viewBox of \"0 0 100 100\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\" and render grid lines + path; dots as HTML divs.\n\nDetails:\n- Container: `<div className=\"relative h-64 w-full pl-14 pb-8\">` (pl-14 = 56px for y labels, pb-8 = 32px for x labels)\n- Inside, plot area: `<div className=\"relative h-full w-full\">` containing:\n  - `<svg className=\"absolute inset-0 h-full w-full\" viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\" preserveAspectRatio=\"none\">`:\n    - grid lines: for each tick y (0..100): `<line x1=\"0\" x2=\"100\" y1={y} y2={y} stroke=\"...\" strokeWidth=\"1\" vectorEffect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" />`\n    - area path: `M x0,y0 L ... L x_last,100 L x_first,100 Z` with fill gradient\n    - line path: `M ...` stroke accent, strokeWidth 2, vectorEffect non-scaling-stroke, fill none, strokeLinejoin round\n  - dots: HTML `<span>` with absolute positioning: left: `${x}%`, top: `${y}%`, translate(-50%,-50%), size 8px, rounded, bg accent, ring.\n- Y labels: HTML absolutely positioned within the plot area but at left of the container: `<span className=\"absolute -left-14 ...\" style={{top: `${y}%`}}>` with -translate-y-1/2.\n- X labels: two spans below the plot: earliest at left-0, latest at right-0.\n\nGradient fill requires an SVG <defs> with linearGradient — works with preserveAspectRatio none.\n\nLet me write it.\n\nValue formatting on y labels: use a compact number format (e.g. 12.3).\n\nLet me write the LineChart component now.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794373065384,"end":1794373065400}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794373065434,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c8f8073276f485864f49","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"import { useMemo } from \"react\";\nimport type { Reading } from \"../api\";\nimport { formatClock } from \"../format\";\n\ntype Point = { t: number; v: number };\n\nfunction compact(value: number): string {\n  if (Math.abs(value) >= 1000) return value.toLocaleString(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: 0 });\n  if (Math.abs(value) >= 100) return value.toFixed(0);\n  if (Math.abs(value) >= 10) return value.toFixed(1);\n  return value.toFixed(2);\n}\n\nexport default function LineChart({\n  readings,\n  unit = \"\",\n  height = \"h-64\",\n}: {\n  readings: Reading[];\n  unit?: string;\n  height?: string;\n}) {\n  const points: Point[] = useMemo(\n    () =>\n      readings\n        .map((reading) => ({ t: new Date(reading.recorded_at).getTime(), v: reading.value }))\n        .filter((point) => !Number.isNaN(point.t))\n        .sort((a, b) => a.t - b.t),\n    [readings],\n  );\n\n  if (points.length === 0) {\n    return (\n      <div className=\"flex h-40 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-dashed border-slate-700 bg-slate-900/40 text-sm text-slate-400\">\n        No readings recorded yet.\n      </div>\n    );\n  }\n\n  const values = points.map((point) => point.v);\n  let minValue = Math.min(...values);\n  let maxValue = Math.max(...values);\n  if (minValue === maxValue) {\n    const pad = Math.max(Math.abs(minValue) * 0.05, 0.5);\n    minValue -= pad;\n    maxValue += pad;\n  }\n\n  const times = points.map((point) => point.t);\n  const minTime = Math.min(...times);\n  const maxTime = Math.max(...times);\n  const timeSpan = maxTime - minTime || 60_000;\n\n  const x = (t: number) => ((t - minTime) / timeSpan) * 100;\n  const y = (v: number) => 100 - ((v - minValue) / (maxValue - minValue)) * 100;\n\n  const linePath = points.map((point, index) => `${index === 0 ? \"M\" : \"L\"} ${x(point.t)} ${y(point.v)}`).join(\" \");\n  const areaPath = `${linePath} L ${x(points[points.length - 1].t)} 100 L ${x(points[0].t)} 100 Z`;\n\n  const ticks = [0, 25, 50, 75, 100];\n\n  return (\n    <div className=\"w-full\">\n      <div className={`relative w-full pl-14 ${height}`}>\n        {ticks.map((tick) => (\n          <div\n            key={tick}\n            className=\"absolute left-0 w-12 -translate-y-1/2 text-right text-[11px] tabular-nums text-slate-500\"\n            style={{ top: `${tick}%` }}\n          >\n            {compact(maxValue - ((maxValue - minValue) * tick) / 100)}\n          </div>\n        ))}\n\n        <div className=\"relative h-full w-full\">\n          <svg\n            className=\"absolute inset-0 h-full w-full overflow-visible\"\n            viewBox=\"0 0 100 100\"\n            preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"\n            aria-hidden=\"true\"\n          >\n            <defs>\n              <linearGradient id=\"chart-fill\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"1\">\n                <stop offset=\"0%\" stopColor=\"var(--color-accent)\" stopOpacity=\"0.35\" />\n                <stop offset=\"100%\" stopColor=\"var(--color-accent)\" stopOpacity=\"0\" />\n              </linearGradient>\n            </defs>\n            {ticks.map((tick) => (\n              <line\n                key={tick}\n                x1=\"0\"\n                x2=\"100\"\n                y1={tick}\n                y2={tick}\n                stroke=\"currentColor\"\n                strokeWidth=\"1\"\n                vectorEffect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"\n                className=\"text-slate-700/60\"\n              />\n            ))}\n            <path d={areaPath} fill=\"url(#chart-fill)\" />\n            <path\n              d={linePath}\n              fill=\"none\"\n              stroke=\"var(--color-accent)\"\n              strokeWidth=\"2.5\"\n              strokeLinecap=\"round\"\n              strokeLinejoin=\"round\"\n              vectorEffect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"\n            />\n          </svg>\n\n          {points.map((point, index) => (\n            <span\n              key={index}\n              className=\"absolute size-2.5 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 rounded-full bg-accent ring-2 ring-slate-900\"\n              style={{ left: `${x(point.t)}%`, top: `${y(point.v)}%` }}\n              title={`${point.v}${unit ? ` ${unit}` : \"\"} — ${formatClock(new Date(point.t).toISOString())}`}\n            />\n          ))}\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div className=\"mt-1 flex justify-between pl-14 text-[11px] tabular-nums text-slate-500\">\n        <span>{formatClock(new Date(minTime).toISOString())}</span>\n        <span>{formatClock(new Date(maxTime).toISOString())}</span>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/components/LineChart.tsx"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/src/components/LineChart.tsx","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/components/LineChart.tsx","time":{"start":1794373065395,"end":1794373065408}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8f81aac001t3yCz8TuiHbn5j","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","messageID":"msg_1c8f7de92001SgSJnqk0aqPJLf"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794373065434,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8f81ac4001hztr5NYXx5AwN6","reason":"tool-calls","messageID":"msg_1c8f7de92001SgSJnqk0aqPJLf","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":40168,"input":819,"output":1254,"reasoning":1390,"cache":{"write":0,"read":36705}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794373078319,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8f84cfb001i32Ow6SnHig1JN","messageID":"msg_1c8f81ad1001UVUAJIQ8gOYIH5","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794373078320,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8f84cfe001uaGUY3e9MvqZfI","messageID":"msg_1c8f81ad1001UVUAJIQ8gOYIH5","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"text","text":"<think>Now the SensorCard component and pages.\n\nSensorCard: props sensor, onClick/link to detail.\n\n```tsx\nexport default function SensorCard({ sensor }: { sensor: Sensor }) {\n  return (\n    <Link to={`/sensors/${sensor.id}`} className=\"group block rounded-2xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-5 transition hover:border-accent/60 hover:bg-slate-900\">\n      <div className=\"flex items-start justify-between gap-3\">\n        <h3 className=\"text-lg font-semibold text-slate-100\">{sensor.name}</h3>\n        <span className=\"rounded-full bg-slate-800 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs text-slate-400\">{sensor.owner}</span>\n      </div>\n      <div className=\"mt-4 flex items-end gap-2\">\n        <span className=\"text-4xl font-semibold tabular-nums text-slate-50\">{formatValue(sensor.last_value)}</span>\n        <span className=\"pb-1 text-sm text-slate-400\">{sensor.unit}</span>\n      </div>\n      <dl className=\"mt-4 space-y-1 text-sm text-slate-400\">\n        <div className=\"flex gap-2\"><dt>Location</dt><dd className=\"text-slate-300\">{sensor.location || \"—\"}</dd></div>\n        <div className=\"flex gap-2\"><dt>Updated</dt><dd><TimeAgo iso={sensor.last_updated} /></dd></div>\n      </dl>\n    </Link>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nNote `bg-accent` — with Tailwind v4 @theme, `--color-accent` generates `bg-accent`, `text-accent`, `ring-accent`. Good. `ring-slate-900` default ring color — with v4, `ring` uses currentColor by default unless specified. I set `ring-2 ring-slate-900` — fine.\n\nAlso note in Tailwind v4, `size-2.5` works.\n\nThe card's \"how long ago it was updated\" uses TimeAgo which ticks every second.\n\nNow the pages.\n\nDashboard page:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function Dashboard() {\n  const { username, ready, signIn, signUp, signOut } = useAuth();\n  const [sensors, setSensors] = useState<Sensor[]>([]);\n  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);\n  const [error, setError] = useState<string | null>(null);\n\n  const load = useCallback(async () => {\n    try {\n      const result = await api.listSensors();\n      setSensors(result.items);\n      setError(null);\n    } catch (err) {\n      setError(err instanceof Error ? err.message : \"Failed to load sensors\");\n    } finally {\n      setLoading(false);\n    }\n  }, []);\n\n  useEffect(() => {\n    void load();\n    const timer = window.setInterval(() => { void load(); }, 10_000);\n    return () => window.clearInterval(timer);\n  }, [load]);\n```\n\nForms: AuthPanel (sign in / register), SensorForm (register sensor), ReadingForm (post reading).\n\nI'll create components:\n- components/AuthPanel.tsx — shows both forms when signed out.\n- components/SensorForm.tsx — register a sensor (name, unit, location) + onCreated callback.\n- components/ReadingForm.tsx — post a reading: select sensor (owned by user) + value.\n\nWhere to show SensorForm/ReadingForm? On the dashboard for signed-in users. Also on the sensor page the owner can post a reading (a simpler inline form).\n\nLet me write these components with a consistent style:\n\nInput classes: \"w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-slate-100 placeholder-slate-500 outline-none focus:border-accent focus:ring-2 focus:ring-accent/30\"\n\nButton primary: \"rounded-lg bg-accent px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-950 hover:bg-accent/90 disabled:opacity-50\"\nButton secondary: \"rounded-lg border border-slate-700 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-200 hover:border-slate-500 hover:bg-slate-800 disabled:opacity-50\"\n\nI'll define these as string constants in a shared file to avoid repetition: src/ui.ts exporting `inputClass`, `primaryButtonClass`, `secondaryButtonClass`, `cardClass`, `labelClass`.\n\nNow write AuthPanel:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function AuthPanel() {\n  const { signIn, signUp } = useAuth();\n  const [mode, setMode] = useState<\"signin\" | \"signup\">(\"signin\");\n  ...\n}\n```\nI'll render two forms in a grid: \"Sign in\" and \"Create account\" side by side (both always visible). That satisfies \"Registration and sign-in forms\".\n\nEach form: username, password, submit button, error message, success message.\n\nAfter successful sign-in, show a message \"Signed in as X\".\n\nDashboard layout:\n\n```\n<div className=\"min-h-screen bg-slate-950 text-slate-100\">\n  <header>...</header>\n  <main className=\"mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-8 space-y-8\">\n    {error banner}\n    {!ready ? loading : username ? <SignedInPanel/> : <AuthPanel/>}\n    <section>\n      <div className=\"flex items-center justify-between\">\n        <h2>Sensors</h2>\n        <span>auto-refreshes every 10s</span>\n      </div>\n      grid of cards\n    </section>\n  </main>\n</div>\n```\n\nThe header: brand \"Sensor Dashboard\", right side: if username → \"Signed in as <username>\" + Sign out button; else → \"Not signed in\" (the forms are below).\n\nLet me write Layout as part of App with a Header component in components/Header.tsx.\n\nSensor page:\n\n```tsx\nexport default function SensorPage() {\n  const { id } = useParams();\n  const [sensor, setSensor] = useState<Sensor | null>(null);\n  const [readings, setReadings] = useState<Reading[]>([]);\n  const [total, setTotal] = useState(0);\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nLoad sensor + readings (limit 100). Poll every 10s too (nice to have). The spec says \"the page refreshes every 10 seconds\" for the dashboard; I'll poll on the sensor page too.\n\nOwner actions: if username === sensor.owner → post reading form + delete with confirmation.\n\nDelete flow: `const [confirming, setConfirming] = useState(false)`. Button \"Delete\" → setConfirming(true) → panel with \"Confirm\" and \"Cancel\". On confirm → api.deleteSensor(id) → navigate(\"/\").\n\nLet me write all files now.\n\nAlso App.tsx: Routes with Layout wrapper.\n\nLet me write the ui.ts constants file and components.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794373078270,"end":1794373078289}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794373078320,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_01a1c8f83cdf7062a06b123c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"export const inputClass =\n  \"w-full rounded-lg border border-slate-700 bg-slate-950 px-3 py-2 text-sm text-slate-100 placeholder:text-slate-500 outline-none transition focus:border-accent focus:ring-2 focus:ring-accent/30\";\n\nexport const labelClass = \"mb-1 block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-400\";\n\nexport const primaryButtonClass =\n  \"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-accent px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-950 transition hover:bg-accent/85 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-accent/40 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50\";\n\nexport const secondaryButtonClass =\n  \"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-slate-700 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-200 transition hover:border-slate-500 hover:bg-slate-800 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-slate-600 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50\";\n\nexport const dangerButtonClass =\n  \"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-rose-600 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition hover:bg-rose-500 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-rose-400 disabled:cursor-not-allowed disabled:opacity-50\";\n\nexport const cardClass =\n  \"rounded-2xl border border-slate-800 bg-slate-900/60 p-5 shadow-lg shadow-black/20\";\n\nexport const errorTextClass = \"text-sm text-rose-400\";\nexport const successTextClass = \"text-sm text-emerald-400\";\n","filePath":"/workspace/frontend/src/ui.ts"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/frontend/src/ui.ts","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"frontend/src/ui.ts","time":{"start":1794373078277,"end":1794373078296}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8f84d000013gBGBehPOmUHDP","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","messageID":"msg_1c8f81ad1001UVUAJIQ8gOYIH5"}}
