{"type":"text","timestamp":1794373155212,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8f97971001cLSAtkZxTKFgUy","messageID":"msg_1c8f96a710019KMEGAtWgf6hdH","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"text","text":"<think>Now let's run the full stack locally: start gunicorn serving the backend with the built frontend on port 8000, and curl the endpoints.\n\nLet me run it in the background and test with curl.\n\nNote: gunicorn from pip (27.0.0) is installed; the Docker image uses 26.2.0. Fine for local testing.\n\nCommand: cd /workspace && gunicorn --bind 127.0.0.1:8000 --pythonpath backend app:app --daemon? Let me run it with nohup in background and then curl.\n\nCareful about the data dir: it will create /workspace/data/app.db. That's the real data dir; I should clean it up before finishing (or leave it? The .dockerignore excludes data/*.db from the image, but the data dir in the repo would be committed... The task says persistent data lives under ./data. Leaving an empty data dir with a test DB isn't great. I'll delete the data dir contents at the end).\n\nLet me run the server.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794373155185,"end":1794373155208}}}
