{"type":"text","timestamp":1794373194465,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8fa12d0001XP4WGwKsBsvJdh","messageID":"msg_1c8fa05bb001zb3u3Mi4lAOo8W","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"text","text":"<think>The repo has a .gitignore? Let me check — node_modules and dist show as untracked, meaning there's no .gitignore. I should add a .gitignore for node_modules, dist, data, __pycache__. That's good practice. Let me check if there's an existing .gitignore.\n\nActually `git status --short` shows `?? frontend/node_modules/` meaning untracked (not ignored). I'll add a .gitignore.\n\nNow, let me do the jsdom smoke test. First install jsdom withoutsaving.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794373194448,"end":1794373194462}}}
