{"type":"text","timestamp":1794373235531,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8fab338001kvYafzw96mfft4","messageID":"msg_1c8fa9db7001b62cZsjQJ1W1PJ","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"text","text":"<think>Vite 8 uses rolldown. I'll use vite's programmatic build API to bundle the smoke entry.\n\n```js\nimport { build } from \"vite\";\nawait build({\n  configFile: false,\n  logLevel: \"error\",\n  build: {\n    lib: { entry: \"src/smoke_entry.tsx\", formats: [\"es\"], fileName: \"smoke_bundle\" },\n    outDir: \"smoke-out\",\n    emptyOutDir: true,\n    minify: false,\n    rollupOptions: { external: [] },\n  },\n  plugins: [react()],\n});\n```\n\nThe output would be at smoke-out/smoke_bundle.js (ESM). Since package.json has \"type\": \"module\", the .js file is ESM. Good.\n\nNeed @vitejs/plugin-react for JSX transform (or esbuild/oxc handles .tsx automatically with the react-jsx automatic runtime — vite's default esbuild/oxc config uses jsx: 'automatic' for React? Not by default; the react plugin sets it. I'll include the plugin.\n\nLet me rewrite the smoke testto use vite build.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794373235512,"end":1794373235527}}}
