{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794373250786,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c8fadf3e73bbb2b6de3d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/frontend && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re, pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"smoke_test.mjs\")\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\"globalThis.navigator = window.navigator;\", \"Object.defineProperty(globalThis, \\\"navigator\\\", { value: window.navigator, configurable: true });\")\ns = s.replace(\"globalThis.navigator = dom2.window.navigator;\", \"Object.defineProperty(globalThis, \\\"navigator\\\", { value: dom2.window.navigator, configurable: true });\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"patched\")\nPY\nnode smoke_test.mjs 2>&1 | tail -40","workdir":"/workspace/frontend"},"output":"patched\nPASS dashboard heading\nPASS sensor card name\nPASS sensor card owner\nPASS latest value\nPASS unit\nPASS location\nPASS null value sensor\nPASS auth forms\nPASS guest hint\nfile:///workspace/frontend/smoke_test.mjs:135\nglobalThis.location.pathname = \"/sensors/1\";\n                             ^\n\nTypeError: Cannot set properties of undefined (setting 'pathname')\n    at file:///workspace/frontend/smoke_test.mjs:135:30\n\nNode.js v24.22.1\n","metadata":{"output":"patched\nPASS dashboard heading\nPASS sensor card name\nPASS sensor card owner\nPASS latest value\nPASS unit\nPASS location\nPASS null value sensor\nPASS auth forms\nPASS guest hint\nfile:///workspace/frontend/smoke_test.mjs:135\nglobalThis.location.pathname = \"/sensors/1\";\n                             ^\n\nTypeError: Cannot set properties of undefined (setting 'pathname')\n    at file:///workspace/frontend/smoke_test.mjs:135:30\n\nNode.js v24.22.1\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/frontend && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport re, pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"smoke_test.mjs\")\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace(\"globalThis.navigator = window.navigator;\", \"Object.defineProperty(globalThis, \\\"navigator\\\", { value: window.navigator, configurable: true });\")\ns = s.replace(\"globalThis.navigator = dom2.window.navigator;\", \"Object.defineProperty(globalThis, \\\"navigator\\\", { value: dom2.window.navigator, configurable: true });\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"patched\")\nPY\nnode smoke_test.mjs 2>&1 | tail -40","time":{"start":1794373248036,"end":1794373250759}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8fae41e001s6DXLZGvUscz6C","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","messageID":"msg_1c8fad80d001EwkQ5O0jiBZ2yt"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794373250786,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8faeeca001mXTtw69Vw7NkT6","reason":"tool-calls","messageID":"msg_1c8fad80d001EwkQ5O0jiBZ2yt","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":60404,"input":223,"output":177,"reasoning":0,"cache":{"write":0,"read":60004}},"cost":0}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794373255500,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8fb0133001Gqhxq71R3I8SyV","messageID":"msg_1c8faeedc001r28XoGa6Vo2272","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1794373255500,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"id":"prt_1c8fb0136001wNRgZPwB8cBZoG","messageID":"msg_1c8faeedc001r28XoGa6Vo2272","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","type":"text","text":"<think>The dashboard checks pass. The second part fails on `globalThis.location.pathname` (no global location in Node). Let me remove that line (the second JSDOM's URL already sets the path for MemoryRouter initialEntries). Wait — in the smoke entry, I use `window.location.pathname` for MemoryRouter initialEntries. In the second run, the bundle is imported fresh with the new global window (dom2), so window.location.pathname = \"/sensors/1\". But React's module registry caches the module — importing with \"?second\" query creates a new module instance for the entry, but its imports (react, react-dom) are cached from the first import. That's fine (React is reused). However, `createRoot` from react-dom/client cached — fine.\n\nBut careful: the entry's `document.getElementById(\"root\")` refers to the new global document. Good.\n\nLet me remove the `globalThis.location.pathname` line.\n\nAlso note the second bundle import: `pathToFileURL(bundlePath).href + \"?second\"` — the URL with a query string. Dynamic import with a query creates a distinct module instance. Good.\n\nOne issue: the app's api.ts uses `window.localStorage` — in the second DOM, localStorage is a different instance and won't have the token. I set `window.localStorage.setItem(...)` on the FIRST dom's window (before replacing globalThis.window). I need to set the token on dom2's localStorage instead. Let me restructure: create dom2, then set dom2.window.localStorage token.\n\nLet me patch: remove the globalThis.location line, and set the token on dom2.window.localStorage.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794373255478,"end":1794373255495}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794373258889,"sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01a1c8fafb177255a5d1252f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/frontend && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"smoke_test.mjs\")\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace('window.localStorage.setItem(\"sensor-dashboard.token\", \"good\");\\nglobalThis.location.pathname = \"/sensors/1\";\\n', '')\ns = s.replace('globalThis.cancelAnimationFrame = dom2.window.cancelAnimationFrame.bind(dom2.window);',\n              'globalThis.cancelAnimationFrame = dom2.window.cancelAnimationFrame.bind(dom2.window);\\ndom2.window.localStorage.setItem(\"sensor-dashboard.token\", \"good\");')\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"patched\")\nPY\nnode smoke_test.mjs 2>&1 | tail -30","workdir":"/workspace/frontend"},"output":"patched\nPASS dashboard heading\nPASS sensor card name\nPASS sensor card owner\nPASS latest value\nPASS unit\nPASS location\nPASS null value sensor\nPASS auth forms\nPASS guest hint\nPASS signed in username\nPASS sign out button\nPASS sensor page title\nPASS chart svg\nPASS readings table\nPASS owner forms\n\nAPI calls: GET /api/sensors, GET /api/sensors/1, GET /api/sensors/1/readings?limit=200, GET /api/me\n\nSMOKE TEST PASSED\n","metadata":{"output":"patched\nPASS dashboard heading\nPASS sensor card name\nPASS sensor card owner\nPASS latest value\nPASS unit\nPASS location\nPASS null value sensor\nPASS auth forms\nPASS guest hint\nPASS signed in username\nPASS sign out button\nPASS sensor page title\nPASS chart svg\nPASS readings table\nPASS owner forms\n\nAPI calls: GET /api/sensors, GET /api/sensors/1, GET /api/sensors/1/readings?limit=200, GET /api/me\n\nSMOKE TEST PASSED\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/frontend && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"smoke_test.mjs\")\ns = p.read_text()\ns = s.replace('window.localStorage.setItem(\"sensor-dashboard.token\", \"good\");\\nglobalThis.location.pathname = \"/sensors/1\";\\n', '')\ns = s.replace('globalThis.cancelAnimationFrame = dom2.window.cancelAnimationFrame.bind(dom2.window);',\n              'globalThis.cancelAnimationFrame = dom2.window.cancelAnimationFrame.bind(dom2.window);\\ndom2.window.localStorage.setItem(\"sensor-dashboard.token\", \"good\");')\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"patched\")\nPY\nnode smoke_test.mjs 2>&1 | tail -30","time":{"start":1794373255487,"end":1794373258870}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_1c8fb01390016uAFQT1H816Wts","sessionID":"ses_e370b5ae4ffe9rbeud9vtYO6Dm","messageID":"msg_1c8faeedc001r28XoGa6Vo2272"}}
